# Advent of Code 2020 day 8: a handheld console that runs a tiny program and
# never terminates. Report the accumulator just before an instruction repeats.
#
# The instruction set is a declared sum type, which is what makes this pleasant:
# `advance` cannot forget an opcode, and adding a fourth one to the declaration
# turns every match on it into an error until that case is handled too.
Op is Nop Earth | Acc Earth | Jmp Earth

arg line is line through earths through first else 0

read line is
  ward line through words through first else ""
    "acc" : Acc (arg line)
    "jmp" : Jmp (arg line)
    _ : Nop (arg line)

program is Source through lines where (l gives gt 0 (len l)) as read

at n is program through drop n through first

step pc acc seen is pick (member seen pc) acc (advance pc acc (insert seen pc))

advance pc acc seen is
  ward at pc
    Stilled : acc
    Held (Nop _) : step (add pc 1) acc seen
    Held (Acc n) : step (add pc 1) (add acc n) seen
    Held (Jmp n) : step (add pc n) acc seen

step 0 0 (circle [])
